libcdr fixes for nitroview (scripts/get-deps.sh applies this after downloading):
- open paths (polylines) are not filled: CorelDRAW fills only closed ones
- text frames and artistic text keep their rotation; artistic text is anchored at its
  transformed origin (the first baseline at the alignment point), not a bounding box guess
- "CMYK100" colour strings (CorelDRAW 2022) were read as white
- objects on hidden layers (layer flag 0x100, e.g. the switched-off layers of an imported
  PDF) are skipped, as in CorelDRAW and its PDF export
- no ICU: code pages through iconv, UTF-16 and UTF-8 decoded here; without a charset (and for
  ANSI / DEFAULT / East Asian ones, which old Hungarian files use too) windows-1250 when the
  text has o/u with double acute, else windows-1252
- CorelDRAW 5 texts (one byte per character) were read as UTF-16
- CorelDRAW 5 bitmaps came out turned by 180 degrees

